+## 48.2 - (Greatly Enhanced and Fixed) Kish city of gilgamesh AI building a theatre instead of a hindu temple despite having unhappy citizens (and health room to grow otherwise anyways etc), and theatre not giving any reliable happiness (almost anything else would have been much better), fixed by fixed by correcting the happiness building formula in our pre-check in CvCityAI::AI_buildingValue, and in particular replacing the too broad and unreliable CvCity::getAdditionalHappinessByBuilding with our own AI_strictAdditionalHappy anyways etc
+
+See screenshots and files about/related(ing? Anyways etc) to this issue in this [google drive folder link](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1xNaTDpRHsdh4YBG176V6pPtnGnbMvL7D?usp=sharing).
+
+This is a nice enhancement to our original pre-checks in `CvCityAI::AI_buildingValue`, as i noticed recently (as of now but anyways etc) but anyways etc that kish city of gilgamesh AI builds a theatre yet is unhappy and would have greatly benefited of a hindu temple instead (theatre unhappiness is not reliable as it is related to culture slider).
+
+The city had enough health room to grow, and was btw nicely surrounded by many grassland tiles, so it was a big mistake to build a theatre here rather than almost anything else.
+
+By digging a bit in our pre-checks, i have found that the logic for identifying happiness buildings is there, but slightly flawed/misleaded/mistaken if i may say in this case i mean but anyways etc, as it relied on base advciv +/- civ4's `CvCity::getAdditionalHappinessByBuilding` that was counting many things, as i asked chatgpt 5 about it and told it about this issue and that we don't want to count extravagant as in hard to get or not relevant to early survival happiness modifiers or effects like the culture slider one, useless in the early game and if not going cultural too, but we want to correctly identify immediate happiness buildings. So now with the help of chatgpt 5 i added to use instead for our pre-checks but anyways etc the new `AI_strictAdditionalHappy` that is limited to most important sources of happiness from buildings (includes bonuses we have, check code there for details and if accurate as is provided by chatgpt 5 i mean but anyways etc).
+
+Also, i rectified the `iEffectiveFood` formula into an additional (no pun but anyways etc...) as of now `iEffectiveFoodAfterBuiltHappy` variable instead for our as of now happiness buildings pre-check(s) but anyways etc so that we add to our food reserve the food we would gain from making the unhappy citizens happy after our building is built. For example, if our building gives 1 happiness in total (including relevant bonuses and all if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc), we'd gain 2 food in our calculation (as each citizen consumes 2 food if i'm not mistaken, is not strictly accurate as there's no guarantee we have high enough food tiles remaning to work, still anything is better than unhappy citizens so count it as such). As a result, we hopefully no longer mistakenly block our nice pre-check of not building the happiness building if food is low (as food would become naturally higher in most/almost all cases but anyways etc as/after the unhappy citizen works tiles instead or does whatever or not or yes or etc but anyways etc).
+
+As a result of these changes and tweaks, it seems we get very very good results!!!
+
+But first, before the changes (existing screenshots between 275 and 278), starting from turn 100 save file to turn 150, kish city of gilgamesh ai is size 10 with one unhappy citizen, trying to build a theatre, which is useless, and has both hill grassland tiles not worked and not chopped (since pop is capped so this is due to our lazy improve cities code i guess so maybe fine or not too bad anyways etc).
+
+After the changes (existing screenshots between 279 and 280 anyways etc), we instead build a few real happiness buildings that are seemingly no longer blocked, which are:
+
+- walls (since in our mod as of now walls give +1 happiness if leader is protective which i think gilgamesh is if i'm not mistaken anyways etc)
+- colosseum (a bit inefficient per hammer cost but the happiness helps grow since we have health room anyways etc)
+- market (very good!! Gilgamesh has elephants bonus so it is great to increase happiness and all)
+
+Thanks to these it seems, kish city is now pop 13 instead at turn 150 (resuming from same save file at turn 100)!!! Which is tremendously better, both very nice hill grassland tiles are worked and improved since we have the population to accomodate them(/these? Anyways etc), and interesting thing is kish city switched from 3 scientists ebfore changes at pop 10 to now 3 merchants at pop 13 (the slider is 100% commerce too), so some code written by someone or many people or not xd leverages the market being built and goes for merchants which is more efficient than scientists here since we have no library after our changes but have a market so better use it!! I would have never thought of skipping library to build a market to gain happiness and then switch to merchant economy xd, that's super smart!!! Our production is still good, but city much better, and much better longterm potential evne if we have slightly less untis as a result but are still the military leader at turn 150 (would be worth even if we lost quite a bit of power but is fine in such case).
+
+So all in all seems like a very good safe and balanced change that should make AI much stronger especially at middle game and city growing!! But check to be sure anyways etc.
+
